Hi!

On 15/10/2018 18:03, Dan Rue wrote:
> [...]
>
> - Wiki.kernelci.org is still a problem. Ana will move over the last bits to the
>    new wiki. Dan changed mailing list link to the correct location, anyway.
>    - Imported images
>      https://github.com/kernelci/kernelci-doc/wiki/Architecture-Overview

I took some time today and I've migrated everything I found still 
relevant into the GitHub wiki plus some other minor updates.

Now this is done, I'd like to raise a couple of ideas that we should 
consider eventually:

* Update https://kernelci.org/faq/ or move that to the wiki. The first 
question "What is kernelci.org?" and the license should be, IMHO, quite 
clear already at https://kernelci.org/

* I'm happy with the GitHub wiki but it pains me it doesn't have any 
search option. Trying to see if we can continue using the wiki and 
export it to somewhere we can use search would help with this. The idea 
I have in mind is something like https://readthedocs.org/

Ana


